Mitoko gave her blessing with a smile, even going so far\nas to prepare us a feast.%K%P
美都子露出了笑容。\n祝福着我们。\n为我们做了一桌好菜。%K%P
The table nearly gave out under the weight of all our\nfavorite dishes being piled on top of it -- like a last\nsupper of sorts -- while Mitoko's cheerful voice filled\nthe otherwise still and silent room.%K%P
那一天的餐桌上，像是最后的晚餐，\n不大的桌子上，摆满了我们爱吃的菜，\n餐桌上充满着美都子的欢声笑语。%K%P
That's right... It was covered in my favorite dishes.%K%P
没错…都是我们爱吃的菜。%K%P
All the dishes that Mitoko had been forcing on me for the\nsake of a \dmore balanced diet\d were completely gone from\nthe menu.%K%P
美都子一直所说的『为了健康』啊『营养平衡』啊，\n这些理念都被那天菜单上锦上添花的点心给华丽地排除了。%K%P
In that moment, we stopped being -family-, and instead\nbecame -guests- at her house.%K%P
那时开始的我们…\n已经成了美都子心中的『客人』。%K%P
