%LC木下
\dI just wanted to remind you of the mountain of papers on\nyour desk still waiting to be signed. Mr. Yoshimura claims\nto have left sticky notes to mark the important parts,\nhoping to help speed up the process.\d%K%P
「今天早上积压的裁决书，请您处理一下吧。\n芳村先生用纸书签标记过了，所以很方便…」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dAh, that... I'm sorry.\nI'll finish them up by five.\d%K%P
「啊啊…抱歉。\n等到５点钟再说…」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\d...Has something been bothering you as of late, Ms.\nSawashima?\nIf I didn't know any better, I'd be worried that you were\nlovesick.\d%K%P
「…最近怎么了啊，泽嶋小姐？\n这样简直就像是得了相思病啊？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\d...If even you're saying that, I imagine the entire\noffice is gossiping about it as we speak.\d%K%P
「…既然你都这么说了，\n是向办公室里的谁打听过这种传闻了吗？」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dThat's right. I'm always the last one to hear anything.\d%K%P
「对啊。\n我在公司里，是消息最不灵通的一个」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dI meant that you were the main source of these things...\nbut whatever. I have to admit, I'm being little more than\na complete waste of a salary at the moment.\d%K%P
「也说明你是强力的散播源头啊…嘛，算了。\n的确，这样下去，我看起来就更像吃闲饭的了」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dGet a grip on yourself, please! You're making it look\nlike you're utterly helpless without Mr. Yoshimura\naround.\d%K%P
「请您振作一点哦？\n只是因为芳村先生不在身边，\n就变得如此懒散，很让人困扰的」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫緒
\d...So? What about it?\d%K%P
「…那还有呢？」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dYou mean your lovesickness?\d%K%P
「相思病的话题吗？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dNo. Do you happen to know where this Mr. Yoshimura of\nyours could be? I haven't seen him around at all lately.\d%K%P
「不是。\n芳村最近去哪儿了？\n完全玩儿起了失踪啊」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dEh? You mean those weren't you orders? Mr. Yoshimura has\nbeen on a business trip since last week.\d%K%P
「诶？不是泽嶋小姐的指示吗？\n要让芳村先生一周内都负责出差的？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dI-Is that true...?\d%K%P
「是…是吗？」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dIt is. He appears to have received an interesting deal of\nsorts from the Group itself. Vice Chief Hiragi keeps\nchecking in on an almost daily basis to see if there's any\npromising new project launching.\d%K%P
「嗯，是要去拜访集团内的客户。\n下一个企划快要开始了，\n平木副部长最近也忙得够呛呢」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dWhen did he become so... proactive?\d%K%P
「他是什么时候…这么精神了啊」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dStill, it's weird that you didn't know about this. I\nmean, you had to sign the paper to approve his trip, no?\d%K%P
「可是，泽嶋小姐居然不知道，可真是奇怪啊…\n明明应该有出差结账的…」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dA paper?\d%K%P
「出差结账？」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dYes. You need an approval from the upper branch to take\nany business trips longer than a week. In other words...\d%K%P
「嗯，一周之内的出差，\n要得到直属部长的结账。\n简单说就是这样…」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\d...? Ah...!\d%K%P
「………？\n啊…啊！」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dMs. Sawashima?\d%K%P
「泽嶋小姐？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dYou're right... When did he even...?\d%K%P
「真的啊…什么时候？」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\d...At least try to skim through the papers you sign,\nplease.\d%K%P
「…请您过目一下，自己签字同意的内容」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dYou don't know how shrewd he is...\nHe keeps blindsiding me whenever I let my guard down.\d%K%P
「太巧妙了，那家伙…\n趁我不注意到时候，若无其事地浑水摸鱼」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dNow that I think about it... that's how you ended up\nlosing your personal office as well.\d%K%P
「话说回来…\n您被赶到职员室的时候也是这种感觉吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYes, it's me. It's been a while.\d%K%P
「嗯，是我。\n最近辛苦你了」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dYo, Laid-off. Where are you?\nI haven't seen you around for a while. What's up?\d%K%P
「哦～失业的。现在在哪儿啊？\n最近没见露面，身体可好？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm... I am in what you could say is the rapidly growing\ncapital of central Japan.\d%K%P
「那个…现在我在发展很快的中部地区首府那里…」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\d...Dude, you could've just said it was Nagoya.\d%K%P
「…你直说是名古屋不就得了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHeh, last night I returned to my parents' place for what\nfeels like the first time in ages. It took less than an\nhour by train.\d%K%P
「哎，昨天我到了好久没回去的老家。\n坐电车花了不到一小时」%K%P
No one prepared me dinner, though. Should've expected\nthat.%K%P
不出所料，谁都没有为我准备饭菜。%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dSo, anyway... I'd like to report what I found real\nquick.\d%K%P
「啊，那个…\n关于到昨天为止的报告」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHow did it go? Did you find out anything?\d%K%P
「怎么样？\n找到了吗？」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dWell...\d%K%P
「那个…」%K%P
Yasunaga's voice took on a grim tone.%K%P
八须永君的声音突然低沉了下来。%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dI looked all over Hagimori, including districts other\nthan ours, but no one seems to have ever heard of this\nKagoshima Junichirou character.\d%K%P
「不只是三丁目，\n包括整个东萩守地区，\n果然谁都不知道，那个叫神子岛顺一郎的老先生」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI see... So it's just as I thought...\d%K%P
「原来如此…果然是啊」%K%P
That information only confirmed that I was getting close\nto the truth.%K%P
我在确认了他的答复之后，\n觉得自己又一次接近了事件的核心。%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dJust as you thought...? Oh, so you have the same\nsuspicions as me. That bond is fake, isn't it?!\d%K%P
「果真是…这样啊，\n失业的和我英雄所见略同。\n那个借据是骗人的假货！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNo, it's genuine. I am certain it wasn't falsified, and\nthat Ms. Honoka wrote it in her own hand.\d%K%P
「不，那是真货啊。\n绝对不是伪造的，\n毫无疑问，那是穗香小姐亲笔写下的借据」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dHow do you know?\d%K%P
「为什么这么肯定啊？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI compared the handwriting.\d%K%P
「我比较过了。\n穗香小姐的笔迹」%K%P
I checked the letter she left for Mitoko before\ndisappearing.\nI also checked the writing on Mr. Retired's lease\nagreement.%K%P
以前，我向美都子借过穗香小姐的留条。\n老爷子持有的贷款契约书上的签名。诸如此类。%K%P
They were written by the same person, no doubt about it.%K%P
无论怎么比对，那都和穗香小姐特有的左撇子字体，\n几乎是一模一样。%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dBut then... who's this Kagoshima Junichirou? He was no\nneighbor, that's for sure, so why did he lend her all that\ndough?\d%K%P
「可是啊…那神子岛顺一郎又是什么货色啊？\n如果不是邻居，那为什么说借就借给房东小姐１００万啊？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNo, he was living next door. I'm pretty sure of that.\d%K%P
「不，他是以前的邻居。当时的」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dWhat? You're not making any sense!\d%K%P
「不懂。\n听不懂你说的是那么」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, by the way, is Mr. Kumazaki anywhere near you? There\nwas something I asked him to look into.\d%K%P
「啊，比起那个，熊崎先生现在在吗？\n我有点儿事情，想要他帮助调查一下」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dGimme a sec.\n...Kuma, it's Laid-off.\d%K%P
「啊啊，我叫他过来。\n…小熊，失业的来电话了～」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dI hear you're in Nagoya?\nDon't forget to bring back some unagi pie.\d%K%P
「名古屋？\n赤○饼和鳗○派捎一份儿回来啊」\n※译注：三重县特产赤福饼，静冈县特产鳗鱼派。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat's not even made in Nagoya... Well, that doesn't\nmatter. Anyway, how did it go?\d%K%P
「那不是名古屋特产…嘛，算了。\n话说，怎么样？」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dYeah, about that... You only used me to confirm what you\nalready knew, didn't you?\d%K%P
「什么怎么样不怎么样的…\n你只是为了得到证据，而使唤我的吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm... what are you trying to imply?\d%K%P
「我说…您这是什么意思？」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\d...Hmph, whatever.\nI'll send you a mail today, so be sure to check it out.\d%K%P
「…哼，算了算了。\n今天之内我会给你发邮件的，记得查看」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThank you very much!\nI could never have done this without you!\d%K%P
「谢谢了！\n真是，我没想到你居然这么靠谱」%K%P
I didn't even know what to say... He could probably make a\nfortune if he only found it in himself to work a bit more\nseriously.%K%P
不如说，这个人，\n认真工作起来，能赚不少钱吧。%K%P
Although...\nI suppose I shouldn't be encouraging unlawful behavior.%K%P
不，沾染上什么坏事，果然还是不行。%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\d...Well? I trust you have prepared my compensation.\d%K%P
「…那？\n我说的报酬，你会准备的吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt's all right. I get extra daily wages for business\ntrips that require overnight lodging, so do look forward\nto a generous helping of unagi pie once I get back.\d%K%P
「你不用担心。\n我到外地出差当天就给你备好了。\n名古屋特产，御○饼和鳗○派，敬请期待」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dYou made me work for days and all I get is a bunch of\nsnacks? Besides, not only is that not from Nagoya, it's\nalso a half-assed imitation!\d%K%P
「我帮了你这么大的忙，就送我这些点心啊？\n话说那些非但不是名古屋特产，而且还是胡诌的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut we're friends. Contributing a manuscript to be used\nfor a friend's book -- a friend you have no business\nrelationship with -- was not something you charged for,\nlast time I checked.\d%K%P
「这话说的，我们不是朋友吗。\n非商业伙伴，基本上不需要靠什么白纸黑字的吧？」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dYou still get a free book in exchange, at least!\d%K%P
「不过相对的，你要把那本印刷的书给我！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIn that case, I shall forward you a copy of my report\nonce I am finished. Please note that it will contain\nsensitive information protected by our non-disclosure\nagreement.\d%K%P
「那就听你的了。\n我会把说明资料上的一部分交给您。\n请注意，不要违反保密义务」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dI've already heard about this from the princess...\nYou really do become quite ruthless when it comes to\nwork.\d%K%P
「虽然早就听公主说过了…\n不过一沾工作，你还真就变成恶人了啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell, I have to earn my bread and butter.\d%K%P
「那个，不劳动者不得食嘛」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dYeah, right. I don't see how this is related to your job.\nAt all.\d%K%P
「不过，话虽如此，\n你现在在做着和本业无关的事情吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhat are you talking about? Of course it's related.\d%K%P
「这话怎么说的，那完全有关系啊」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dHuh? But what we're currently looking into...\d%K%P
「可是，咱们现在调查的可是…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt is... related. I will make sure this earns a profit.\d%K%P
「关系大大的有。\n您就等着瞧好吧」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dHahh...\d%K%P
「呼…」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫緒
\dHe's still not back...\d%K%P
「今天也…没回来啊」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dWhat's his problem?\nWhy can't he be there when it counts the most...?\d%K%P
「那家伙搞什么啊…\n这个时候，为什么还不来陪我啊…」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dAh, damn. All the bad thoughts come at once the moment I\nfind myself alone. ...I've got to get a drink.\d%K%P
「啊啊…不行。\n一个人待着，就渐渐考虑起讨厌的事了。\n………不喝一杯果然没有干劲」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dI should just forget everything... about Toko... about\nthe Terrace House Hinosaka, and... about him, too...\nnghm!\d%K%P
「把什么都忘掉吧…\n小都子也好，Terrace House阳之坂也好，\n还有…那个混蛋…啊呜！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm... Why is it so dark in here?\d%K%P
「我说…为什么不开灯啊？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dNghm?! N-Ngh, ngmmmmh!!\d%K%P
「嗯嗯！？\n嗯、嗯～、嗯嗯嗯嗯嗯～！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dH-Himeo?! What happened to you?!\d%K%P
「姬、姫绪小姐！？\n振作一点啊！」%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dKhehh, khehh, khahh... Ugh, I thought I'd die.\d%K%P
「咳咳、咳咳、咳咳咳…\n死、我快要死了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...What is a bottle of whiskey doing here?\d%K%P
「…威士忌？」%K%P
As I approached the little bottle lying under the bed, I\ndetected the sweet scent of cocoa mixed with western\nalcohol.%K%P
掉在床上的小瓶子里，\n飘出了可可与洋酒的甘甜味道。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dI wanted to drink myself to sleep.\d%K%P
「喝多喝醉了，也就能睡着了…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWith a bottle of that size?\d%K%P
「就这一瓶吗？」%K%P
Could you even get drunk off this much...?%K%P
就这么喝着喝着就能喝下去了么。\n多么合乎情理啊…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAnyway, let me return to my initial question. Why are the\nlights off? And not only in this room, but everywhere else\nin the house, too.\d%K%P
「那回到一开始的提问，\n为什么如此昏暗？\n而且不止是房间连玄关都是」%K%P
I could get inside because I had a spare key, but being\nunable to see my own feet, I ended up getting lost and\nwandered around half the house before I finally reached\nthis room.%K%P
我有大门的钥匙，所以也进得去，\n可是在移动中，伸手不见五指，\n就这样到达了房间真是不容易啊。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dI... I needed some time to think.\d%K%P
「我啊…考虑了一些事情」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWhat about the fact that switches don't even work?\d%K%P
「为什么不把灯打开呢？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dIt's been like this for three days now.\nI've already gotten used to living in the dark, though.\d%K%P
「三天前开始就这样。\n眼睛已经差不多习惯了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThey cut the electricity in your house!\nWhy on earth don't you pay the bills?!\d%K%P
「哎，难道停电了吗！？\n为什么不交上电费啊！」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dYou think I have the money for that right now?\d%K%P
「你觉得，现在的我能拿得出电费吗…？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh, that's right...\d%K%P
「啊啊，说的也是啊…」%K%P
Mr. Sasaki held onto both her cash and credit cards.%K%P
现金也好，信用卡也好，都保管在佐佐木先生那里。%K%P
And according to my investigation...%K%P
那个大概，\n不在我的调查范围之内…%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dStill, this is weird... I thought things like electricity\nwere automatically charged from my card.\d%K%P
「即便这样也很奇怪啊…\n这个月的费用难道都用完了吗」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat's... do you have a flashlight?\d%K%P
「那…你有手电筒吗？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dI don't know where most things are in this house.\d%K%P
「不知道扔在哪里了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...I'll go look. Maybe I can find some candles, at\nleast.\d%K%P
「…找找吧。\n找到蜡烛也可以」%K%P
Could it be possible that she was more helpless at running\nher life than even myself?%K%P
她不会是…\n生活能力比我还要差劲吧？%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOkay. I can finally see your face. ...I'm back.\d%K%P
「有了…这下我终于能看清姬绪小姐的脸蛋了。\n…我回来了」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dW-Welcome ho-- Ah.\d%K%P
「欢、欢迎回来………啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHm? Himeo?\d%K%P
「？姫绪小姐？」%K%P
Her charming features, illuminated by the candlelight,\nseemed to light up for a moment before instantly\ndisappearing again.%K%P
微明的灯光照亮了她可爱的脸庞，\n只是一瞬间的光芒闪耀，\n之后，又急剧地熄灭了下去。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\d...Why did you come here?\d%K%P
「…为什么你要来这里啊？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm, because I'm back from my business trip?\d%K%P
「我出差回来了」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dTh-That's not what I'm asking...\d%K%P
「问、问的不是那个…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHere you go, some local furaibo chicken wings. I prefer\nthose over the yamachan style myself.\d%K%P
「给你，这是当地土产，风○坊的鸡翅。\n比起山○，我更喜欢这个」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dThey're cold!\nI only eat these when they're freshly fried!\d%K%P
「这不是凉的吗！\n我只吃炸鸡块啊！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWe could microwave them... if you had electricity.\d%K%P
「那，要热一热吗…呃，\n停电了吧」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dWhy do you keep avoiding the subject?\d%K%P
「为什么要这样岔开话题啊…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWell... because you keep going along with my jokes.\d%K%P
「那…是你在拒绝我吧」%K%P
I found that part of her endearing, even back when she\nstill hated me.%K%P
以前，被她讨厌的时候，\n我倒是挺喜欢这样逗她的。%K%P
The fact I couldn't bring myself to dislike her must've\nhad something to do with the relationship between our\nhometowns. Probably.%K%P
无论我做了什么，她都不会真的怨恨我，\n这或许是我们之间，微妙的同乡意识作怪吧。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dWhy... Why did things have to turn out like this...?\nAhh... uah, uah... uaaahhh...!\d%K%P
「为什么…为什么变成这样了啊…\n呜呜、呜、呜…呜啊啊啊啊…啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHimeo... please don't cry.\d%K%P
「姫绪小姐…别哭了」%K%P
I placed my hand on her head.%K%P
我抚摸着泣不成声的她的头发。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\d...Stay away!\d%K%P
「啊…不要靠近我」%K%P
She hesitated for a brief second before brushing my hand\noff.%K%P
然后，她甩开我的手，\n那个瞬间，有一丝犹豫。%K%P
But that was enough time for our bodies to come into\ncontact... and for that nostalgic scent of hers to tickle\nmy nostrils.%K%P
因为我的手，一瞬间与她紧紧相连了。\n她的味道，真是令我怀念不已。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dLook, Osamu... Osamu...\nWe're... we're... we're finished... uaaahhh...!\d%K%P
「呐，理先生…理先生。\n我们、我们…已经结束了啊…呜呜呜呜呜」%K%P
Yet she still tried to reject me with words.%K%P
可是，在行动上给了我可乘之机的她，\n在言语上，还是对我摆出了一副拒绝的态度。%K%P
...I'd never heard such an unwilling declaration of a\nbreakup.%K%P
…这么恋恋不舍的口气，\n说来还是头一回呢。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI don't feel that way, though.\nI'm hoping to stay by your side.\d%K%P
「我可从来没那么想。\n我啊，从今往后也要和姬绪小姐在一起」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dE... Eh?!\d%K%P
「诶…诶诶！？」%K%P
And that was what made me use a somewhat forceful tone,\ndespite not being at work.%K%P
正因为如此，就算在工作以外的时候，\n她还是对我吞吞吐吐，言不由衷。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dB-But that's... no... Wh-What are you even saying, Osamu?\nThere's nothing we can do about it. It's impossible.\d%K%P
「怎、怎么能、怎么能…\n你、你在说什么啊理先生，\n那种事，肯定是不行的啊」%K%P
After all, a single line was enough to light up her face\nwith anticipation, regardless of what her mouth said.%K%P
…不管怎么说，只有这句话，\n她憔悴得声泪俱下，喃喃说出的这句话，\n一下子让我情绪高涨了起来。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAnd what if we separate? You think one of us could just\ngo back and stay with Mitoko? And she'd be okay with\nthat?\d%K%P
「就算分开了又能怎样？\n我们中的其中一个再回到美都子身边去吗？\n那样做了，美都子就会原谅我们吗？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dTh-That's...\d%K%P
「那、那个…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAnd most important of all... Do you think Mitoko would be\nable to forgive herself if that really happened?\d%K%P
「还有，这是最关键的…\n如果那样，美都子难道不会责备自己吗？」%K%P
If we separated -because of her-, we would likely never\nsee her smile again. Not around us, at any rate.%K%P
如果我们因为『为了美都子』而分手了，\n那个女孩，恐怕再也不会对我们露出微笑了吧。%K%P
That was the only kind of future I could see stemming from\nthis -- for us, there was no turning back. Not anymore.%K%P
眼见那么悲伤的未来，\n我们已经没有退路了。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dB-But... Toko loves you... Osamu...\d%K%P
「可、可是，小都子对你…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI love her too. I want to be with her.\d%K%P
「我也最喜欢美都子了。\n想和她一直在一起」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\d...!\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut I don't want to see you like that, either.\n...Actually, could you not cry over a mere example?\d%K%P
「但是，我也不希望姬绪小姐像现在这样伤心。\n…话说，只是这种程度而已，别哭了啊」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫緒
\dUah... uahh... uahhhh!\d%K%P
「呜…呜呜呜、呜呜呜呜呜～啊！」%K%P
I felt that her mental age was far below Mitoko's.%K%P
这个人…\n精神年龄远比美都子要低啊。%K%P
Well, that was exactly why I couldn't just leave her be.%K%P
嘛，正因为这样，我就更放不下她了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHimeo... come here.\d%K%P
「来，姫绪小姐…到这边来吧」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫緒
\dUaaaahhh... Osamu... Osamu...!\nI... I... I don't know what to do...!!\d%K%P
「呜呜呜呜呜呜呜～，理、理先生、理先生…\n我、我…该、怎么办…啊」%K%P
Himeo, who had tried to reject barely a minute ago, jumped\ninto my embrace the moment I opened my arms.%K%P
刚刚还拒绝了我的姫绪小姐，\n朝着我张开的胸口，\n狠狠地飞扑了过来。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt's okay. Everything's going to be fine.\nThis is hardly the end. In fact, our fight has only just\nbegun.\d%K%P
「没事儿，没事儿了…\n我们的关系还没完呢。\n真正的战斗，才刚刚开始」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dUah, uahh, sniff... uah...\nWh-What do you mean, our fight?\d%K%P
「呜、呜呜、呜…呜、呜…\n战、战斗…是什么意思？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWe have an enemy.\nA powerful enemy that means to inflict great harm upon the\nthree of us.\d%K%P
「我们面前出现了敌人…\n威胁我们三人的，强大的敌人」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dH-Huh? Are you talking about that... Nishikawa person?\d%K%P
「诶、诶…？\n也就是，上次的…姓西川的男人？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNo, he're merely the puppet of a puppet of a puppet.\nOur enemy is far above, at the top of that food chain.\d%K%P
「不，他不过是傀儡的傀儡的傀儡。\n他上头的上头的上头…才是真正的大ＢＯＳＳ」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dIs it really someone that important...?\d%K%P
「那、那么厉害的对手，吗…？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYes. A tremendous foe.\nAnd one that is very close to us, too.\d%K%P
「嗯，是个非常难对付的敌人。\n而且，他就近在眼前」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\d...?\d%K%P
「…？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dKagoshima Junichirou is still alive.\nAnd it's him pulling the strings in all of this.\d%K%P
「神子岛顺一郎还活着。\n这次在背后操纵着阴谋的，就是他」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dKagoshima... Junichirou?\d%K%P
「神子岛…顺一郎？」%K%P
I traveled all across the country over the past week to\nfind his trail.%K%P
这一周里，我东跑西颠，终于抓住狐狸尾巴了。%K%P
A friendly neighbor who'd lent a million yen without\nconsidering to even form an official bond.%K%P
不假思索地就借出了１００万，\n而且连借据都不准备写的好人邻居。%K%P
A person shrouded in mystery whose name no one in the\nneighborhood could remember.%K%P
而且，是个在东萩守居住的老人们，\n都从来没有听说过的，谜之男人。%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dEh? Eh? But Toko said she didn't know a person like\nthat.\d%K%P
「诶、诶？\n可是小都子，说不认识那个人…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIn that case... could you please lend me your phone for a\nbit? I'll call him.\d%K%P
「那…你把手机给我。\n我来和他本人联络」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dWhat about your phone?\d%K%P
「你的手机呢？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm... it doesn't have any charge left.\d%K%P
「那啥…我的手机没电了」%K%P
That, of course, was a lie, seeing how...%K%P
这无疑是个谎言。\n因为…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dUm... Oh, here it is.\d%K%P
「那个………哦，找到了」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dEh?\d%K%P
「诶？」%K%P
I didn't know what Kagoshima Junichirou's personal phone\nnumber was. That was information reserved for only a\nselect few.%K%P
我不知道神子岛顺一郎的电话号码。\n知道的，只有其中一个人物。%K%P
In other words, only a handful of people in the world\nwould have had his phone number saved in their contacts.%K%P
可能存在着那个人物的通讯录。%K%P
%LC???
%LC？？？
\dHimeo? Why are you calling me so late?\d%K%P
「姬緒吗？\n怎么了，这么晚打电话过来？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dGh?! Eh? Eh? Ehh?!\d%K%P
「啊！？\n诶？诶？诶诶！？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dPleasure to make your acquaintance, Mr. Kagoshima\nJunichirou... or should I say, Mr. Sawashima Junpei. My\nname is Yoshimura Osamu. I am working as your daughter's\nsecretary.\d%K%P
「初次见面，神子岛顺一郎先生…不，泽嶋顺平先生。\n我在您女儿的手下担任秘书，名字叫芳村」%K%P
One such example would be... that very person's own\ndaughter.%K%P
比如…对，比如是亲女儿的通讯录。%K%P
